,title,link,text,language,family
0,Tirahi language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tirahi_language,"Tirahi is a nearly extinct if not already extinct Indo-Aryan language spoken in a few villages in the southeast of Jalalabad in the Nangarhar Province of eastern Afghanistan. It is spoken by older adults, who are likewise fluent in Pashto.",Tirahi,Indo-European
1,Tirahi - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tirahi,Tirahi (Pashto: تيراهي) are Indo-Aryan people who are native and original inhabitants of Tirah valley.,Tirahi,Indo-European
2,Tirahi language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/tirahi_language,"Tirahi is a nearly extinct Dardic language belonging to the Indo-Aryan branch of the Indo-European language family, historically spoken by a small community in eastern Afghanistan. It is classified wi.",Tirahi,Indo-European
3,Tirahi — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/tirahi,"Grierson documented Tirahi as a distinct language spoken by local communities in Tirah, emphasizing its archaic Indo-Aryan features that differentiate it from the surrounding Pashto dialects, thereby indicating the Tirahi as original inhabitants predating Pashtun migrations.",Tirahi,Indo-European
